---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import FigMap from '../components/figures/FigMap.astro';
import FigBottleneck from '../components/figures/FigBottleneck.astro';

const bookUrl = 'https://calendar.notion.so/meet/cameronearloliver/qc3y04oud';

const steps = [
  { n: '01', title: 'I map how the company makes money', body: "Every way it gets a customer, and everything it does to keep them. This alone usually surfaces growth that's being left on the table." },
  { n: '02', title: 'We see what it takes to deliver', body: 'What each part actually needs to run: people, technology, resources. Where growth is quietly capped.' },
  { n: '03', title: 'We find the one thing to fix first', body: 'The bottleneck holding the number back. I help the team knock it out, then we go find the next one.' },
  { n: '04', title: 'We keep it running', body: 'A simple rhythm the team can hold on their own, so the gains show up in the next board pack and the one after.' },
];
---

<Layout
  title="For Private Equity | Growth Map"
  description="You backed the plan. When a portfolio company falls behind, it's almost never where you think. I'm an operator you send in to find what's holding growth back and fix it with the team you already have. Book a call."
  canonicalPath="/investors"
>
  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="px-6 py-20 md:py-28">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[900px]">
      <p class="text-[14.5px] font-semibold text-moss">For private equity</p>
      <h1 class="font-display mt-6 text-4xl leading-[1.06] text-ink sm:text-5xl md:text-[56px]">
        One of your companies is <em>behind plan.</em>
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-[56ch] text-lg leading-relaxed text-fern">
        The thesis was right. The team is working hard. The growth just isn't showing up, and from the board seat it's tough to see why. I get in the trenches, find what's actually holding it back, and fix it with the team you already have.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-8">
        <a href={bookUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-block rounded-full border border-ink bg-ink px-8 py-4 text-[15px] font-semibold text-parchment transition-opacity hover:opacity-90">
          Book a call
        </a>
        <p class="mt-3.5 text-sm text-fern">Tell me where a company's stuck. A free 30-minute call.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE TWO THINGS -->
  <section class="bg-parchment-deep px-6 py-20 md:py-28">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[1000px]">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl leading-tight text-ink md:text-[40px]">
        No matter the industry, every business does <em>two things.</em>
      </h2>
      <div class="mt-10 grid items-stretch gap-5 md:grid-cols-[1fr_auto_1fr]">
        <div class="rounded-[18px] bg-white shadow-[0_2px_10px_rgba(20,38,26,.07)] p-8">
          <p class="font-display text-5xl leading-none text-moss">1</p>
          <h3 class="font-display mt-4 text-2xl text-ink">Get customers</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-fern">It has to find and win people who buy.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center">
          <span class="text-[15px] text-muted">then</span>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-[18px] bg-white shadow-[0_2px_10px_rgba(20,38,26,.07)] p-8">
          <p class="font-display text-5xl leading-none text-moss">2</p>
          <h3 class="font-display mt-4 text-2xl text-ink">Serve those customers</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-fern">It has to deliver, and keep them coming back.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-9 max-w-[70ch] text-lg leading-relaxed text-fern">
        When a company is behind plan, the answer is always in one of those two. Before you put in more capital or more people, it's worth knowing which one is actually broken.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE MAP -->
  <section class="px-6 py-20 md:py-28">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[1100px]">
      <p class="text-[15px] font-semibold text-muted">Where I start</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-7 text-3xl leading-tight text-ink md:text-4xl">It all starts with the map.</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-[54ch] text-lg leading-relaxed text-fern">Understanding how the company actually makes money, before touching anything.</p>
      <div class="mt-10 space-y-10">
        {steps.map((st, i) => {
          const Fig = [FigMap, null, FigBottleneck, null][i];
          return (
            <div class:list={["grid items-center gap-6 md:gap-12 md:grid-cols-2", i % 2 === 1 && "md:[&>*:first-child]:order-2"]}>
              <div class="flex gap-5">
                <p class="font-display text-[17px] text-moss">{st.n}</p>
                <div>
                  <h3 class="font-display text-[22px] leading-tight text-ink">{st.title}</h3>
                  <p class="mt-1.5 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-fern">{st.body}</p>
                </div>
              </div>
              {Fig && (
                <div class="rounded-[18px] bg-white shadow-[0_2px_10px_rgba(20,38,26,.07)] p-4">
                  <Fig />
                </div>
              )}
            </div>
          );
        })}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- HOW I WORK -->
  <section class="bg-parchment-deep px-6 py-20 md:py-28">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[900px]">
      <p class="text-[15px] font-semibold text-muted">How I work</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-7 text-3xl leading-tight text-ink md:text-4xl">
        I don't come in to take over.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-[64ch] text-lg leading-relaxed text-fern">
        The fastest way to break a company is to send someone in who announces they're in charge. I don't do that. I earn the team's trust, work through the people already there, and the founder stays the founder. When it's running on its own, I hand it back and step out.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- AI -->
  <section class="px-6 py-20 md:py-28">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[900px]">
      <p class="text-[15px] font-semibold text-muted">One more thing</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-7 text-3xl leading-tight text-ink md:text-4xl">
        I build the tools, too.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-[64ch] text-lg leading-relaxed text-fern">
        A lot of the growth I find comes from taking repetitive work off the team, so they do more without more headcount. I build those tools myself. It's an accelerant on a company that already has the fundamentals right, not a substitute for getting them right first.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CLOSE -->
  <section class="bg-parchment-deep px-6 py-20 md:py-28">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[900px]">
      <p class="text-[15px] font-semibold text-muted">Fit</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-7 text-3xl leading-tight text-ink md:text-4xl">
        Let's be straight about it.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-[62ch] text-lg leading-relaxed text-fern">
        This works when the company actually wants the help and there's a real number to move. If it's not a fit, I'll tell you on the first call, and we don't waste each other's time.
      </p>
      <a href={bookUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="mt-8 inline-block rounded-full border border-ink bg-ink px-8 py-4 text-[15px] font-semibold text-parchment transition-opacity hover:opacity-90">
        Book a call
      </a>
      <p class="mt-3.5 text-sm text-fern">A free 30-minute call.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
